# nr-office-ooxml-docx-snapshot: integration fragment

New module `snapshot_docx` of the existing crate mixdog-ooxml (port of portable-snapshot-docx.mjs: snapshot_docx,
docx_body_model, append_docx_block, has_adjacent_tables, separate_adjacent_tables, close_trailing_table,
numbering_level_format, docx_pictures). No protocol method, service or SERVICE_PENDING name belongs to it, and no new
dependency edge (it uses mixdog-js, mixdog-office-base and serde_json, already listed by the crate).

## native/core/crates/mixdog-ooxml/src/lib.rs

After `pub mod slide_shapes;` / `pub mod snapshot_shared;` add:

    pub mod snapshot_docx;

(The crate doc comment may list "the docx snapshot ([`snapshot_docx`])" beside the other modules.)

## native/core/fixtures/MANIFEST.json

In the "sets" list, at its place in set-name order (the list is sorted by set name: in mig/int today after the entry of
office-measure and before office-stats; after office-sheet-xml if another fragment of the wave adds that set first), add:

    {
      "command": "node benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-snapshot-docx.mjs --tree <tree>",
      "fileCount": 1,
      "manifest": "office-snapshot-docx/MANIFEST.json",
      "manifestSha256": "e8710147efb30fed6f072320e80ba512d5eb9608bded2a9a440aefad511414c5",
      "recorder": "benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-snapshot-docx.mjs",
      "set": "office-snapshot-docx",
      "totalBytes": 601472
    }

The set's own MANIFEST.json lists golden.json (601472 bytes) and records the product identity of the tree the recorder ran
against; recompute manifestSha256 with `sha256sum` if the file is written again.

## Later consumers

`docx_body_model` and `append_docx_block` (and `has_adjacent_tables`, `separate_adjacent_tables`, `close_trailing_table`)
are the functions the docx writers (the write-core and write-pages tasks) take; `docx_pictures` is the reading the
accessibility audit shares with the snapshot.
